Generating functionality sections, also known as feature or capability descriptions, involves breaking down complex systems into smaller, manageable pieces. In an overview section, you typically see high-level statements describing what the system does. Estimation is often used to provide a rough estimate of time required for each task.

- **Overview Section:** When creating an overview section related to functionality (e.g., a web application or API), include any relevant metadata such as:
  - Title: The title should be descriptive and concise.
  - Description: Provide a brief summary of the system, including its purpose and key features.
  
- **Functional Requirements:** Break down each functional requirement into smaller tasks that can be implemented. Include all necessary details for each task, such as:
  - Functionality description
  - Estimated time required (ESTIMATED TIME)
  - Assumptions made during estimation

 
